  "id": "taco/3dclouds",
  "title": "Cloud 3D - GOES-16 Tropical Cyclones Finetuning Dataset",
  "description": "Cloud3DTACO is a large-scale remote sensing dataset pairing 2D multispectral geostationary imagery from GOES-16, Himawari-8/9, and MSG/SEVIRI with co-located 3D vertical cloud profiles from the CloudSat radar. This finetuning subset focuses on tropical cyclones, covering structures such as eyewalls and rainbands derived from IBTrACS best-track records. Approximately 500,000 samples are stored as Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs following FAIR principles.",
